<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch16-differential-forms-wedge" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Differential Forms and the Wedge Product</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Chapters 13 and 15 introduced work and flux integrals, and Chapter 12 introduced pullbacks of area and volume forms. This chapter gives these examples a common algebra: covectors measure tangent vectors, wedge products measure oriented pairs and triples, and pullbacks express those measurements in parameters.</p>
  </introduction>

